# TolongLabs Proprietary Source-Available Licence 1.0

Copyright (c) 2026 TolongLabs. All rights reserved.

## 1. What this licence is

This licence applies to the software, source code, documentation, designs and other material
in this repository, and every version of them published with this licence (together, the
**Work**).

Any part of the repository that is identified as owned by someone else (for example in a NOTICE
or third-party licence file) stays under its own licence, and this licence does not apply to it.

The Work is proprietary. Publishing it on GitHub or anywhere else does not make it open
source, and does not give anyone any right except the rights written in this licence.

By downloading, copying, running, modifying or sharing the Work, or making any other use of it
that needs a licence, you accept this licence. If you have not accepted it, you have no licence,
and any of those acts may infringe copyright (clause 10.1).

## 2. Definitions

**TolongLabs** means the Founders acting together under the name "TolongLabs", and includes
any company or other body to which the Founders later transfer the rights in the Work.

**Founders** means the founders of TolongLabs recorded in its private schedule (clause 3.1),
or any person who replaces one of them under the Founders' private arrangements.

**Council** means the governing council (board) of TolongLabs, made up of the Founders. The Council
decides under the Founders' private arrangements, which are confidential and are not part of
this licence. A written notice issued in the name of the Council is conclusive evidence, as
between TolongLabs and you, that the Council has made the decision stated in it.

**Author** means a person listed in the AUTHORS file of this repository whose listing the
Council has approved. **Co-author** means an Author who contributed jointly with another Author.

**Contribution** means anything a person submits for inclusion in the Work, including code,
text, images, comments, pull requests and patches.

**Disclosed Materials** means copies of any part of the Work, and other TolongLabs materials
such as pitch decks, demos, prototypes, specifications, designs and data, that TolongLabs gives
you outside this repository in connection with a possible business deal.

**Personal Use** means use by an individual for their own study, learning, hobby projects or
private, non-commercial purposes.

**Academic Use** means use for study, teaching or non-commercial research at a school, college,
university or research institute, including publishing academic papers or theses about the
Work.

**Commercial Use** means any use of the Work, or of anything made from it, that is intended
for or directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation, whether direct or
indirect. It includes, without limitation: selling, licensing or renting the Work; using it to
provide a paid or advertising-funded product or service; using it inside a business,
including internal business operations; using it in work done for a client or employer; and
using it to train, fine-tune or evaluate a commercial artificial intelligence system.
Research or teaching that is paid for or sponsored by a commercial organisation in return for
rights in the results, or that is aimed at a commercial product, is Commercial Use.

**Financial Year** means the period from 1 January to 31 December, or any other accounting
period the Council adopts in writing and tells the Authors about.

**You** means any person or organisation that receives or uses the Work, other than TolongLabs.

## 3. Ownership and authorship

3.1 All copyright and other intellectual property rights in the Work, in every country, belong
to TolongLabs, except where a written document issued by the Council says otherwise. Until
TolongLabs is registered as a separate legal entity, those rights are owned jointly by the
Founders as partners carrying on business as TolongLabs. The Founders' full legal names are
recorded in a private schedule kept by TolongLabs and will be produced in any proceedings where
they are needed.

3.2 TolongLabs alone decides who may use the Work, for what purpose, in which field, in which
territory and on what terms. TolongLabs may grant, refuse, limit, condition or end any
permission for any field of use.

3.3 The names of the Authors and Co-authors are recorded in the AUTHORS file. You must not
remove, hide or change any copyright notice, author name or licence notice in the Work.

3.4 Nothing in this licence transfers ownership of the Work, or any part of it, to you.

3.5 A licence or permission given by one Founder alone, and not issued in the name of the
Council, has no effect between you and TolongLabs.

## 4. What you may do without a separate licence

4.1 Free of charge and without asking, you may view, run, copy and modify the Work for:

(a) Personal Use;

(b) Academic Use; and

(c) evaluating, for up to 30 days, whether to ask TolongLabs for a commercial licence,

in each case with no Commercial Use. For Academic Use, you may also share copies with your own
students, teachers and research colleagues, provided this licence goes with every copy and
nobody pays for them. Evaluation under paragraph (c) is not Commercial Use, but it does not
include production use, delivery to a client or any use that earns money.

4.2 Except as allowed to an Author by a consent under clause 6, you must not, without TolongLabs' prior
written licence:

(a) make any Commercial Use of the Work;

(b) distribute, publish, sublicense, sell, rent or make the Work available to anyone else,
except as clause 4.1 allows or through the forking functions that GitHub's own terms of
service allow for a public repository;

(c) use any modified version or derivative work of the Work for anything other than the uses
in clause 4.1;

(d) remove or bypass any licence check, key or technical protection in the Work; or

(e) use the name "TolongLabs", its logos or any Author's name to promote anything.

4.3 Any copy of the Work that you are allowed to make must keep this licence file and every
copyright, author and licence notice exactly as they appear in the Work.

4.4 GitHub notice. If this repository is public, GitHub's terms of service allow GitHub users
to view and fork it inside GitHub. That permission comes from GitHub's terms, not from this
licence, and gives no right to use any fork for any purpose that this licence forbids.

4.5 Nothing in this licence limits any right the law gives you that cannot be excluded by
agreement.

## 5. Commercial licences

5.1 Commercial Use of the Work is not permitted by default. It is allowed only under a written
licence issued in the name of the Council. No Founder, Author, employee or agent can give
that permission orally or by conduct.

5.2 Requests for a commercial licence go to: tolonglabs@gmail.com.

## 6. Commercial use by Authors

6.1 An Author may make Commercial Use of the Work as a whole only for a specific use that
TolongLabs has consented to under this clause 6, and only through a client deal made under
clause 6B. Any consent is a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable licence. It does
not allow the Author to give, sell, license or host the Work, or a copy of it, for any other
person or company outside a deal made under clause 6B. A company that wants to use the Work
itself needs its own licence under clause 5.

6.2 Request. The Author must send TolongLabs a written request at tolonglabs@gmail.com describing the
use, the product or service, who it is for and the planned start date. Each new product, client
or significant change is a separate use and needs its own consent.

6.3 Other Authors. TolongLabs will promptly tell the other persons listed in the AUTHORS file
of the Work at the time of the request (the **other Authors**) about the request. Each of them
may vote for or against it by writing to TolongLabs within 14 days after the request. The
requesting Author does not vote. Votes are sent only to TolongLabs and are confidential; the
requesting Author is told only the result. All deadlines in this clause 6 are counted in
Malaysian time. A refused request may be made again as a new request.

6.4 TolongLabs decides. TolongLabs has one vote, cast by the Council. The Council will take the
other Authors' votes into account, but TolongLabs' vote decides the request. If TolongLabs
consents, consent is given even if every other Author votes against. If TolongLabs refuses,
consent is refused even if every other Author votes for.

6.5 Form and deadline. A consent has effect only if it is in writing and issued in the name of
the Council. If no consent is given within 14 days after the request, the request is refused.

6.6 No reasons. The Council is not required to give any reason for refusing, limiting or
revoking a consent. The Council's deliberations, votes and reasons are confidential to the
Council and will not be disclosed, unless a formal written agreement signed by the Author and
issued in the name of the Council expressly requires reasons to be given.

6.7 Revocation. The Council may revoke, suspend or limit any consent, or all of an Author's
rights under this clause 6, at any time, in whole or in part, by written notice sent by email
to that Author's email address on record. The revocation takes effect when the notice is sent, or on any later date stated in it.

6.8 Wind-down. After revocation, the Author must stop the Commercial Use concerned within the
reasonable period stated in the revocation notice, which will be at least 14 days unless the
Council and the Author agree otherwise in writing.

6.9 A revocation under this clause 6 is not a breach of this licence by the Author. Clause 10.2
does not apply to the wind-down period in clause 6.8.

6.10 Revocation does not remove the Author's name from the AUTHORS file and does not affect the
Author's moral right to be identified as an author.

6.11 A formal written agreement signed by the Author and issued in the name of the Council may
change any part of this clause 6, 6A or 6B for that Author, and if so it prevails over this
licence.

## 6A. Authors' share of profits

6A.1 For each Financial Year of TolongLabs, each Author is entitled to a share of the Net Profit
equal to that Author's Contribution Percentage of the Net Profit.

6A.2 Combined cap. The shares of all Authors together must not exceed 25% of the Net Profit for
that Financial Year. The 25% is a single cap shared among all Authors, not a cap for each
Author. If the Authors' shares would together exceed 25%, each Author's share is reduced in
proportion so that the total is 25%.

Example: three Authors have Contribution Percentages of 20%, 10% and 10%. Together that is 40%,
which is over the cap, so their shares become 12.5%, 6.25% and 6.25% of the Net Profit (25% in
total). If instead their percentages were 10%, 5% and 5% (20% in total), each would receive
exactly their own percentage, because the total is under the cap.

6A.3 **Contribution Percentage** means the part of the whole Work that the Author contributed,
as a percentage, decided by the Council in writing and taking into account the code, design,
documentation and other work the Author contributed. Where Co-authors contributed jointly,
the Council divides that contribution between them. The Council may review it when the Work
changes. The Council records each Author's Contribution Percentage in writing, with its date,
no later than 60 days after the end of each Financial Year. Each Author is told their own
Contribution Percentage. The Council's decision is final unless it contains an obvious error,
without limiting the right to refer a dispute to arbitration under clause 14.

6A.4 **Net Profit** means the money TolongLabs actually receives in a Financial Year from
commercial licences, sales, client deals and other Commercial Use of the Work, after deducting
all costs, expenses, taxes and reasonable reserves related to the Work, including payments to
Authors under clause 6B, as shown in TolongLabs' accounts. Money paid or distributed to the
Founders is not a cost and is not deducted. Reserves must relate to the Work, and any reserve not
used is added back in a later Financial Year. Net Profit is never less than zero.

6A.4A Prize money, awards and other winnings from hackathons, competitions or any other events,
whether in cash or in kind, are not covered by this licence, and this licence does not apply to
them.

6A.5 TolongLabs will pay each Author's share within 90 days after the end of each financial
year, with a short statement showing the Net Profit, the Author's Contribution Percentage, the
total of all Authors' Contribution Percentages (without names) and any reduction under the cap.
Payments are made in Ringgit Malaysia, after any tax TolongLabs must withhold by law and normal
bank charges.

6A.5A Accounts check. Once in each Financial Year, an Author may ask, at the Author's own cost,
for an independent registered accountant to check that the Author's share and any reduction
under the cap were worked out correctly. The accountant is agreed between the Author and
TolongLabs, or, if they do not agree within 14 days, chosen by TolongLabs. The accountant reports
only whether the calculation is correct and the amount of any error, and keeps all other
information confidential. If there is an error, TolongLabs pays any shortfall within 30 days.
The Author pays the accountant's fee in every case.

6A.6 Payments to an Author for client deals are made under clause 6B and are separate from
this profit share.

6A.7 If the Council revokes a consent or an Author's rights under clause 6, the Author's profit
share stops from the date the revocation notice is sent, or from any later date stated in the
notice or agreed with the Author in writing. The Author keeps the profit share for Net Profit received
before that date.

6A.8 The Founders are part of TolongLabs and are not Authors for the purposes of this clause 6A.
How TolongLabs pays or distributes money to the Founders is a private matter for the Council and
is not part of this licence.

6A.9 The profit share is payment for the Author's contribution. It does not make any Author a
partner in TolongLabs, give any Author a say in how TolongLabs is run, or allow any Author to
act for or bind TolongLabs. The Author has no share in any loss or capital of TolongLabs.

6A.10 Amounts an Author has already earned under clause 6A or 6B stay payable after any
revocation, termination or new version of this licence.

## 6B. Client deals and payments to Authors

6B.1 All Commercial Use of the Work for a client, including any use by an Author under a
consent, goes through TolongLabs. The contract with the client is signed by TolongLabs and by
each Author who does the work.

6B.2 If an Author refuses, or fails without good reason, to attend or sign the client contract
when TolongLabs asks, the Author is treated as having excluded themselves from that deal.
TolongLabs may go ahead without them, and the Author has no right to any payment from that deal.
This affects only payment from that deal and does not affect clause 6A.

6B.3 The client pays TolongLabs only. The Author must not ask for or accept any payment from the
client for that deal. Any payment the Author receives from the client is held for TolongLabs and
must be passed to TolongLabs within 7 days.

6B.4 TolongLabs pays the Author the amount or percentage stated in the consent for that deal,
issued before the work starts. If the consent states none, the Authors who do the work on that
deal share 25% of TolongLabs' Net Receipts from that deal equally between them, so the total for
all of them is 25%.

6B.5 **Net Receipts** means the money TolongLabs actually receives from the client for that deal,
after deducting the documented direct costs and taxes of that deal, each deducted once. Net
Receipts are never less than zero.

6B.6 TolongLabs pays the Author within 90 days after it receives each payment from the client,
with a short statement showing how the amount was worked out. Payments are made in Ringgit
Malaysia, after any tax TolongLabs must withhold by law and normal bank charges.

6B.7 TolongLabs pays the Author only out of money it actually receives from the client. It will
make reasonable efforts to collect payment, but owes the Author nothing for any amount the
client does not pay.

6B.8 Revocation of a consent does not affect the Author's payment for client money TolongLabs
receives for work the Author did before the revocation took effect.

6B.9 A formal written agreement signed by the Author and issued in the name of the Council may
set any other amount or terms, and if so it prevails over this clause 6B (see clause 6.11).

