## 13. Interpretation

13.1 This licence is to be read so as to give the fullest protection the law allows to the
rights of TolongLabs as copyright owner, and secondly to the Authors and Co-authors.

13.2 No rule of interpretation will apply to read any part of this licence against TolongLabs
because TolongLabs prepared it.

13.3 Any right not expressly granted in this licence is reserved to TolongLabs.

13.4 If any part of this licence is invalid or unenforceable, it will be applied to the
greatest extent allowed, and the rest of the licence continues in force.

13.5 TolongLabs may publish a new version of this licence. Each version of the Work is
governed by the licence version published with it, unless TolongLabs agrees otherwise in
writing. A consent given under clause 6 continues for the use it was given for until it is
revoked. No new version reduces any amount an Author has already earned without that Author's
written agreement.

13.6 Order of documents. If documents conflict, they apply in this order: (1) a formal written
agreement signed by you and issued in the name of the Council; (2) a signed TolongLabs Evaluation
and Confidentiality Agreement, for Disclosed Materials and confidential information; (3) a signed
TolongLabs Contributor Notice; (4) this licence.

13.7 Language. This licence is written in English. If it is translated, the English version
prevails.

13.8 Transfer to the LLP. TolongLabs may transfer this licence, any consent, any signed agreement
with you, and all its rights and obligations under them, to a limited liability partnership,
company or other body formed by the Founders. You agree to that transfer in advance. Amounts
already earned stay payable by the body that takes over.

13.9 You may not transfer your rights under this licence to anyone else.

## 14. Governing law and disputes

14.1 This licence, and any dispute arising out of or in connection with it or with the Work or
any Disclosed Materials, including any non-contractual dispute, is governed by the laws of
Malaysia, except as clause 14.9 says.

14.2 Where the laws of Malaysia give no clear answer on a point, the law of Singapore and the
decisions of the courts of Singapore may be referred to as persuasive guidance.

14.3 Arbitration. Except as clause 14.9 allows, any dispute between TolongLabs and you arising out of or in connection with
this licence, the Work or any Disclosed Materials will be referred to and finally resolved by
arbitration administered by the Asian International Arbitration Centre (AIAC) in Kuala Lumpur under its
arbitration rules in force when the arbitration starts.

14.4 Place of hearings and seat. All hearings and meetings in the arbitration will be held in
Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, unless TolongLabs agrees otherwise. The legal seat of the arbitration
is Singapore.

14.5 Arbitration law. The parties expressly agree, for the purposes of section 15(1) of the
International Arbitration Act 1994 of Singapore, that the Model Law and Part 2 of that Act do
not apply to the arbitration and that the Arbitration Act 2001 of Singapore applies to it. This
clause 14 (the arbitration agreement) is governed by the law of Singapore.

14.6 Appeal to the Singapore court. You agree in advance, for the purposes of section 49(3)(a)
of the Arbitration Act 2001 of Singapore, that TolongLabs may appeal to the General Division of
the High Court of Singapore on any question of law arising out of an award. Any appeal by you
may be brought only with the permission of that Court. This consent is given now, cannot be
withdrawn, and applies to every appeal by TolongLabs. The parties do not exclude the Court's
jurisdiction under section 49.

14.7 Arbitrator and language. There will be one arbitrator, appointed by the AIAC under its
rules. If the AIAC has not appointed the arbitrator within 30 days after a written request, the
appointing authority under the Arbitration Act 2001 of Singapore may appoint. The language of
the arbitration is English. If this clause 14 conflicts with the AIAC rules, this clause 14
prevails.

14.8 Court proceedings by TolongLabs. Nothing in this clause 14 prevents TolongLabs from going
to the courts of Malaysia, Singapore or any other country, against anyone (including a person
who has agreed to this licence):

(a) for an injunction or other urgent or interim relief;

(b) against a person who has not agreed to this licence; or

(c) to enforce an award or judgment, which may be enforced in any country.

14.9 Court option for TolongLabs. Instead of arbitration, TolongLabs may choose to bring a dispute
before the courts of Singapore, which will then have jurisdiction over it. If TolongLabs makes
that choice, that dispute is governed by the law of Singapore and dealt with under the procedure
of the Singapore courts. TolongLabs makes the choice by starting court proceedings in Singapore
before an arbitration on the same dispute has begun.

